**Matrix Testing with Multiple Consumers**:
When a provider serves multiple consumers with different expectations:
```java
// Provider tests all consumer pacts
@PactBroker(
    host = "${PACT_BROKER_URL}",
    consumers = {"order-service", "inventory-service", "recommendation-service"}
)

// Or test specific consumer versions
hasPactsFromPactBrokerWithSelectors('http://broker', 
    [[consumer: 'order-service', tag: 'prod', latest: true],
     [consumer: 'inventory-service', tag: 'dev', latest: true]]
)
```

**Provider States for Complex Scenarios**:
Setup complex data scenarios before verification:
```java
@State({
    value = "user with ID 123 has orders with specific statuses",
    action = StateChangeAction.SETUP
})
public Map<String, Object> setupUserWithComplexOrders() {
    // Create user, products, orders with specific statuses
    return Map.of("userId", 123, "orderIds", List.of(456, 789));
}
```

**Request Filtering and Authentication**:
Handle authentication in provider verification:
```java
@BeforeEach
void setUp(PactVerificationContext context) {
    context.setTarget(new HttpTestTarget("localhost", port));

    // Add request filter for authentication
    context.getProviderInfo().setRequestFilter(request -> {
        request.addHeader("Authorization", "Bearer test-token");
        return request;
    });
}
```

**Custom Matchers for Flexible Contracts**:
Define custom matching rules:
```java
.willRespondWith()
    .body(new PactDslJsonBody()
        .id()  // Auto-generate ID matching
        .stringMatcher("email", ".+@.+\\..+")  // Regex matcher
        .eachLike("items", 1)  // Array with at least one item
        .decimalType("total", 100.0)  // Type matching, not exact value
    )
```

**Bi-Directional Contract Testing**:
When both services are providers and consumers:
```mermaid
graph LR
    A[Order Service] -->|Consumes| B[Product Service]
    B -->|Consumes| C[Inventory Service]
    C -->|Consumes| A

    A -->|Provides| C
    B -->|Provides| A
    C -->|Provides| B
```

**Contract Testing for Async APIs**:
Testing message queues, WebSockets, or event-driven systems:
```java
// Pact for messages (not HTTP)
@Pact(provider = "product-events", consumer = "order-service")
public MessagePact productCreatedEvent(MessagePactBuilder builder) {
    return builder
        .given("a product is created")
        .expectsToReceive("product created event")
        .withContent(new PactDslJsonBody()
            .uuid("productId")
            .stringType("productName")
            .decimalType("price"))
        .toPact();
}
```

